# Layer Roles (Mandatory)

Each layer has ONE role. Do not let a layer act as another.

## Backend roles

| Role | Location | Allowed | Forbidden |
|------|----------|---------|-----------|
| Controller | `Http/Controllers` | Receive request, call service, return Inertia/JSON/redirect | Queries, validation rules, business rules |
| Form Request | `Http/Requests` | Validation, authorization for input | DB access, business logic |
| Service | `Services/` | Business rules, orchestration, transactions | HTTP, Inertia, Blade/JSX |
| Action | `Actions/` | Single use-case command (create user, import family) | Multiple unrelated use cases |
| Model | `Models/` | Persistence, relations, casts, scopes | HTTP, notifications, complex workflows |
| Middleware | `Http/Middleware` | Cross-cutting HTTP concerns | Domain logic |
| Provider | `Providers/` | Bind interfaces, boot config | Feature business logic |

## Frontend roles

| Role | Location | Allowed | Forbidden |
|------|----------|---------|-----------|
| Page | `pages/` | Layout, Head, page-level data display, Form submit | Reusable UI, complex logic |
| Component | `components/` | Reusable UI, local UI state | API calls, business rules |
| Hook | `hooks/` | Reusable state/effects (theme, mobile) | JSX markup |
| Lib | `lib/` | Pure helpers, constants (`brand-colors`) | React components |
| Type | `types/` | Shared TypeScript interfaces | Runtime logic |

## Dependency direction (strict)

```
Pages → Components → Hooks → Lib
Controllers → Services/Actions → Models
```

Upper layers depend on lower layers. Never reverse (Model must not call Controller).
